---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import NewsletterForm from '../components/NewsletterForm.astro';
import { COLUMN, SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="About" description="What Data Governance Signal is, who it is for and how it works.">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Signal, not noise.</h1>
      <p>{SITE.tagline}</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Data governance professionals are expected to follow regulators in several jurisdictions, new standards, court
        decisions, research and a fast-moving vendor market — while doing their actual job. Most of what is published
        does not matter to them. Some of it matters a great deal.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Data Governance Signal</strong> follows more than fifty carefully selected sources — data protection
        authorities, the European Commission, standards bodies, professional associations, specialist law firms,
        researchers and vendors — and selects what is worth your time.
      </p>
      <h2>What you get with every item</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>A short, original summary</strong> of what happened.</li>
        <li><strong>Why it matters</strong> — the business and governance impact.</li>
        <li><strong>Governance areas affected</strong> and <strong>who should care</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>An importance rating</strong>, from background to critical.</li>
        <li><strong>Links to every source</strong>, with primary sources marked.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Who it is for</h2>
      <p>
        Chief data officers, data governance leads, data stewards and owners, data protection officers, compliance and
        risk professionals, AI governance teams and the consultants who work with them.
      </p>
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        An automated process checks our sources several times a day, removes duplicates and uses AI to assess relevance
        and draft summaries. <strong>Nothing is published without review by a human editor</strong>, who edits,
        approves or rejects every item. Read our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for the details.
      </p>
      <h2 id="editor">The editor</h2>
      <p>
        Every item is reviewed and approved by the editor, who also writes <a href="/monday-signal/">{COLUMN.name}</a>,
        our weekly column. {COLUMN.authorBio}
      </p>
      <p>
        The editor writes under a pen name because they work in the field. The pen name is used consistently, the
        column is clearly labelled as opinion, and where a topic could involve a conflict of interest — for example a
        vendor or organisation the editor has a working relationship with — the column says so.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Tips, corrections and feedback: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="nl"><NewsletterForm /></div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--gutter));
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .prose ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }
  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .nl {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
